Cartesian closed structure: the curry adjunction and the terminal unit system.

<!-- formalization -->

**Instance (`Subsingleton (ApproximableMap V unitSys)`).** There is at most one approximable map into the unit system.

*Proof.* Compare elementwise using uniqueness of the unit element. ∎

**Instance (`Unique (ApproximableMap V unitSys)`).** There is a unique approximable map into the unit system, namely the constant at the unique unit element.

*Proof.* Take the constant map as default and invoke the subsingleton law. ∎

**Definition (`homAdjunction`).** Maps out of a product are order-isomorphic to maps into the function space via curry.

*Proof.* Invoke the curry equivalence. ∎

**Definition (`toUnit`).** The unique map into the unit system is the default of that unique type.

*Proof.* By definition. ∎

**Theorem (`toUnit_unique`).** Every map into the unit system equals the unique map.

*Proof.* Invoke the subsingleton law. ∎
